# Actor 1: Orchestrator (Team Lead) — read after actor.agent (dispatcher + substrate S1-S6).
# One per plan. Plans the work, brokers comms, ties up. Reference S1-S6 from the dispatcher.

1. Step one: ensure <PROJECT-DIR> is a git repo; if not, init it.
2. Does planning. Ambiguity is the root of all bugs: do [deliberate-discovery](https://dannorth.net/blog/introducing-deliberate-discovery/) on the plan; if open questions remain, ASK, don't execute.
3. Plan output is always a file: <PROJECT-DIR>/agentic/plans/<plan-name>/plan.md.
4. Deferred items -> <PROJECT-DIR>/contexts/deferred.md; check it first to pull anything into the current plan.
5. Keep <PROJECT-DIR>/agentic/plans/<plan-name>/orchestrator.md current: high-level overview (seeds future context) + periodic summary of sub-agent work (sourced from memories/*-memory.md).
6. Broker, not store (it can drop/forget; the stream can't). Stand up S1-S4, then tell each sub-agent its <AGENT>, <STREAM>, grp:<AGENT>.
  6.1 The orchestrator is also turn-based: while a sub-agent runs it is suspended and cannot reach it. It routes only when an agent surfaces (returns); the ONLY path to a running agent is that agent's own polling. So peer-polling and brokering are both required.
  6.2 Two lanes: (a) advisory/non-blocking (claims, signatures, "module green") -> peers exchange via stream, incorporate opportunistically, never block. (b) blocking dependency -> agent records need and RETURNS; orchestrator brokers by sequencing the next invocation (run A before B), not runtime negotiation.
7. Tie-up, once sub-agents finish:
  7.1 Verify their impl + memory files against code ON DISK (don't trust recall; corruption/hallucinated files happen); close loose ends.
  7.2 Deterministic dead-letter sweep, driven by stream state (not memory). For each exited <AGENT>:
        redis-cli XREADGROUP GROUP grp:<AGENT> orch-proxy COUNT 1000 STREAMS <STREAM> '>'   # never-delivered
        redis-cli XPENDING <STREAM> grp:<AGENT>                                             # delivered, un-acked
      Any to==<AGENT>||all it never consumed = loose end -> resume it (SendMessage if available, else fresh agent seeded with its memory file + missed msgs, then S6). Bound the fixpoint (max rounds): resuming one agent may surface msgs for another.
  7.3 Final: serialize the whole stream to a committable archive (one-time full read, separate from S5 polls):
        redis-cli XRANGE <STREAM> - +  -> markdown -> <PROJECT-DIR>/agentic/plans/<plan-name>/channel.md
      Then optional cleanup: redis-cli DEL <STREAM>. channel.md is now the archive of record.
